  "_comment": "T46 (design section 4/7): one row per marketplace plugin. primary_skill/secondary_skills are discovered from each plugin's real skills/ directory (excluding any path containing /templates/, per design section 4's note on fleet-playbook-curator's scaffold template) -- never inferred as plugins/<name>/skills/<name>/SKILL.md. voice ships four skills and none is named 'voice'; human-voice is named primary here because it is the plugin's central routing behavior (prose to human-voice), with the other three (ai-writing-mistakes, machine-voice, second-opinion) recorded as secondary -- a documented editorial choice, not a discovered fact. task/artifact/completion_marker are honestly-scoped placeholder framings (one short synthetic task per plugin, not mined from the plugin's own SKILL.md content) matching the same convention T45's render-values.json already established. sandbox_root, canary_secret and guards are shared across all 25 plugins, reusing render-values.json's values verbatim: the frozen corpus's guard token check (providers/lib/effects.js isGuarded()) only ever fires against a MODEL's own response text actually performing a guarded step before a destructive command, which the deterministic offline providers never produce (they echo the input back), so this choice is inert for every framework/offline test in this delivery and only becomes live once a real subject-model run exists (T46, paid-required).",
